#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/set-system-options.md:2
msgid "Set system options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/set-system-options.md:4
msgid ""
"Snap supports a set of system-wide options that allow you to customise your "
"snap environment. See {ref}`System options <reference-operations-system-"
"options>` for which options are supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/set-system-options.md:6
msgid ""
"As with {ref}`Configuration in snaps <how-to-guides-work-with-snaps-"
"configure-snaps>`, these options are changed with the `set` and `get` "
"commands, but with a target of  *system* instead of a specific snap:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/set-system-options.md:8
msgid ""
"snap set system system.timezone=\"Europe/London\"\n"
"snap get system system.timezone\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/set-system-options.md:13
msgid ""
"Configuration options can be unset by either passing their names to the "
"unset command or by adding an exclamation mark (!) to the end of an option "
"name:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/set-system-options.md:15
msgid ""
"$ snap unset system system.hostname\n"
"$ # or\n"
"$ snap set system system.hostname!\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/set-system-options.md:21
msgid ""
"If a setting is part of the system snap, provided by either the core snap or "
"snapd itself, the command syntax will include two instances of _system_, "
"such as with `system.timezone`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/set-system-options.md:23
msgid "snap set system system.timezone=\"Europe/London\"  \n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/set-system-options.md:27
msgid ""
"Typing `snap get system` outputs a top-level view of system-wide option "
"categories which can be added as arguments to view their contents:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/set-system-options.md:29
msgid ""
"$ snap get system\n"
"Key           Value\n"
"experimental  {...}\n"
"refresh       {...}\n"
"seed          {...}\n"
"system        {...}\n"
"$ snap get system experimental\n"
"Key                   Value\n"
"experimental.hotplug  true\n"
"experimental.layouts  true\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/set-system-options.md:42
msgid ""
"The entire set of system configuration options can be dumped as JSON by "
"adding the -d option:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/set-system-options.md:44
msgid ""
"$ snap get -d system\n"
"{\n"
"        \"experimental\": {\n"
"                \"hotplug\": true,\n"
"                \"layouts\": true,\n"
"                \"quota-groups\": true\n"
"        },\n"
"        \"refresh\": {\n"
"                \"last\": \"2017-05-25T09:03:58.664837614+01:00\",\n"
"                \"retain\": 2\n"
"        },\n"
"        \"seed\": {\n"
"                \"loaded\": true\n"
"        },\n"
"        \"system\": {\n"
"                \"hostname\": \"neon\",\n"
"                \"network\": {},\n"
"                \"timezone\": \"UTC\"\n"
"        }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/set-system-options.md:68
msgid ""
"Options are _not visible_ until after they are set. The `snap get` command "
"can then be used to check their state."
msgstr ""
